00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
Hey guys. I'm Abbey Sharpe welcome to another edition of Fertility Files here on Abbey's Kitchen.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.950
Today we'll be talking about a topic that we all love to hate our period

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.830
And, guys, before you click next you might actually learn something about the women in your life,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.570
so I do encourage you to maybe stick around. Now, real talk friends

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.559
women of childbearing age are no stranger to the cramps,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.849
cravings, and mood swings that come with the dreaded time of the month. I've received a lot of questions about this,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:35.130
so today I'm gonna be breaking down the research on the best things to eat during each phase of your

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.420
cycle, so that we can all feel our best. Now before we get into it

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:39.690
of course

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.450
my general disclaimer that the information in this video is for

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.700
education and entertainment purposes only,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:51.689
and you should always speak to a registered dietitian or your health care provider about your unique case.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.949
Okay so let's get into it by starting with the first phase of the menstrual cycle

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.340
the follicular phase. Day 1 of the cycle is marked by the arrival of our favorite red frenemy our

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:09.868
monthly period. Now, this phase involves the shedding of the uterine lining, and depending on your cycle, this may last for approximately

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.460
3 to 6 days.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:18.210
I think we can all agree that we aren't feeling too hot during this phase. Aside from the sexy crime scene in our pants,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.960
we typically feel super tired, sluggish, and

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:27.839
experience painful cramps that make us want to call in sick and chill in the field position for the day.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:33.449
And who exactly is to blame for all of these emotional and physical changes? Our fluctuating hormones of course.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:41.369
At this stage of our cycle the hormones progesterone and estrogen are at their lowest which explains the low energy and overall

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:48.389
sluggishness that women tend to experience. So what can we do from a nutritional standpoint to ease the effects of this phase?

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:55.829
Tip number one - up that iron. Iron is a really important mineral that helps produce red blood cells and

00:01:56.259 --> 00:01:59.729
transports oxygen throughout the body. Because of menstrual blood losses,

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.319
iron deficiency is one of the most common nutritional deficiencies among women of childbearing age.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:11.429
Lower iron levels during menstruation also explains why women typically have low energy and fatigue.

00:02:12.489 --> 00:02:19.768
Therefore women must compensate for the amount of blood being lost from their period by eating more iron rich foods during this time.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.869
So iron rich animal sources include foods like red meat, poultry and fish, and

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:31.799
plant-based sources include fortified cereals, tofu, beans, lentils, and other legumes. Tip number two -

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:37.408
pair it with vitamin C. Vitamin C is an antioxidant that not only helps with immunity,

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:45.239
healthy skin, and wound healing but also helps our bodies to absorb iron even better. Think of vitamin C as iron's

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.140
trusty sidekick or cheerleader that brings out the best in them.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.769
So if you're adding an iron rich meal during that time of the month,

00:02:53.019 --> 00:02:57.689
make sure to pair it with a source of vitamin C like citrus fruits or veggies like bell peppers,

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:03.658
tomatoes or leafy greens. To give you an example, this could look as easy as a bowl of veggie chili

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.159
with a squeeze of lime juice on top or tofu stir-fry with bell peppers.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.159
It's actually an intuitive pairing because these foods just kind of taste good together and

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:19.198
It just proves how smart the body truly is. Tip number three - go decaf.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.099
Just as vitamin C helps to increase the absorption of iron,

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:27.479
there are also certain inhibitors to be aware of that can interfere with iron absorption.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:34.319
Coffee and caffeinated teas, such as green tea and black tea, have an antioxidant substance called polyphenols

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.560
which can decrease the amount of iron the body absorbs.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.729
The other potential downside to caffeine is that it's a vasoconstrictor,

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:45.029
which means it makes the blood vessels in your body

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:49.889
constrict. A lot of women find that this constriction can make their period cramps even worse.

00:03:49.889 --> 00:03:56.069
So for that reason it might be best to stick to herbal tea on those first few days, or at the very least

00:03:56.530 --> 00:04:03.780
spread the caffeine out at least an hour before or after your iron rich meal to help maximize the absorption of iron.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:11.069
Tip number four - get plant powered. A lot of women find that their cramps in these early days of this phase

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.929
so debilitating that they have a really hard time enjoying a full meal.

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:23.279
This is also the time when our bloating and cramps start. So making sure to stay nourished with lighter,

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:28.350
less processed food may help. While salt and fat are both super delicious,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:35.939
you probably inherently know that this isn't probably going to make you feel so great right now because we're already feeling so bloated,

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:43.080
sluggish, and sick. Salt increases water retention which causes bloating and fatty foods increase

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.100
prostaglandin production which can increase contractions aka cramps.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:53.130
So I would really try to focus on recipes with lots of veggies and fruit,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:59.369
especially those that are rich in hydrating water and energizing carbs to help with your waning energy levels.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:05.820
Plus a little bit of some whole grains and legumes. Meals in this phase do not need to be fancy or Instagrammable.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.670
I mean, you're probably really tired and just feel like crap.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:15.390
So be kind to yourself and focus on super simple meals with whole ingredients whenever you can.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.390
Tip 5 - Take a walk.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:22.799
Okay, so during those first few days of your period and the days that follow, your estrogen and progesterone levels are pretty low.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.320
So your stamina might not be so great.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:31.229
But there is some evidence that a little light gentle exercise may play a therapeutic role in

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:37.409
relieving cramps by releasing endorphins which helps improve your mood and relax the body.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.790
Exercise may also provide a distraction from the discomfort of the cramps.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:48.389
So that also is always a good thing. This may or may not be helpful for everyone depending on the severity of your cramps,

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:53.759
but it doesn't hurt to try. Okay, let's jump into Phase two of the menstrual cycle - Ovulation.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:06:00.119
Now at this phase, a new egg begins the process of preparing its descent down the fallopian

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:06.179
tubes to enter the uterus in hopes of meeting a nice little sperm to settle down with. This phase is met with an

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.250
increase in estrogen, testosterone,

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:14.730
follicle stimulating hormone, and luteinizing hormone, which explains why we feel more energized at this point.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.820
So take advantage of this increase in libido, sexual

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:23.010
energy and mood now is your time to work.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:29.129
Tip one - Move in a way that feels good. Because your energy levels are now a lot more balanced in this phase,

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:32.369
you're probably feeling more excited to hit the gym.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:39.840
So hit up some Pilates, weight training, spin class, or what I guess evolution would want us to be doing of course

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:47.189
having sex. Our higher energy levels and brighter mood are a good match for these types of moderate to high intensity

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:55.710
activities. So if you are an active person and this brings you joy, now is the time for it. Tip number two - use

00:06:55.710 --> 00:07:00.509
this energy to prep. Again, because this phase allows for optimal energy levels

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:05.219
this is the best time to get in the kitchen and cook up a storm.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:09.449
So get out your slow-cooker, instant pot, and every casserole dish you own.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.930
This is when you want to do your batch prepping for the week.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:18.959
So chopping up vegetables, cooking proteins, making freezed soups and casseroles for the week.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.190
Go get'em girl.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:21.730
Now,

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:24.809
let's talk about the third and final phase of the menstrual cycle,

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:31.349
the luteal phase. The luteal phase happens when ovulation phase does not result in fertilization

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.289
Aka there ain't no bun in the oven.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:42.780
When this happens, hormone levels decline and we experience the oh so lovely PMS. This may include symptoms like cramps, headaches,

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.300
bloating, mood swings, fatigue, and food cravings. Which brings me to tip number one -

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.250
notice your food cravings. Now, we have all been there

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:58.710
you know, eating chocolate chip cookies and crying over a cheesy rom-com for no real

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:05.699
reason. That, my friends, is the luteal phase aka when PMS hits. But food cravings symptoms are actually

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:12.990
scientifically proven. Research has found our food cravings during the luteal phase are linked to the amount of leptin in our blood.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:20.369
Leptin is the hunger hormone that tells us when we're full and we can stop eating. Studies have actually shown that there may be a

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.560
relationship between leptin and

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:28.860
estrogen hormones and the food cravings that we experience. When leptin and estrogen levels are high during the luteal phase,

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.400
women tend to experience increased cravings

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.950
particularly for sweet carb rich foods. However, when leptin and estrogen levels are low

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:44.819
women may experience fewer cravings. Now, we may not be able to change our leptin or estrogen levels,

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:52.109
but what we can do is listen to our bodies and notice our cravings and any patterns that arise during this phase of menstruation.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:58.139
Do you crave sweet foods or salty foods? Are there certain textures that you prefer? maybe a

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.819
satisfying crunch from a bag of chips or the soft doughiness from a doughnut?

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:04.200
I mean, it's really important

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:10.770
we start to become more aware and mindful of these food cravings in order to assess what it is that your body actually needs.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:13.199
And that brings me to tip number two -

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:19.799
Let yourself have the carbs. As mentioned, research suggests that we tend to crave

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:24.329
Refined carbs during this phase, thanks to PMS. And trust me,

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:28.560
I am all for enjoying that cookie or bowl of chocolate ice cream.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:35.639
But this is a long-ass phase of our cycle and when we're about to lead ourselves into an even more sluggish phase aka

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:41.730
Our period right after, I figure it's ideal to have some really good fuel on board.

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.879
Also, restricting all the carbs right when you're craving them

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:52.020
the most is just going to kick off a massive cookie binge and that is just not gonna leave us feeling too hot either.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:57.360
Now is the time to focus on slow burning but delicious carbs.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:03.149
Maybe make a big batch of overnight oats for breakfast, pick up a hearty seedy bread for lunch, or

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:08.429
roast some sweet potatoes with a little bit of maple syrup and cinnamon for dinner. And when in doubt,

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:12.329
pair that carb with a source of protein and fat to keep those blood sugar

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:18.509
levels even keeled. Tip number three - up the fiber. On a similar note, let's talk about fiber.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.180
Progesterone levels are at an all-time high

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:26.789
during this phase right before your period, and we know that progesterone is one of the major culprits of

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:34.529
constipation. So you're gonna want to sneak in lots of fiber rich whole grains like quinoa, or bran cereal, things like berries,

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.530
or vegetables like broccoli or kale,

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:41.790
flax, beans, and nuts. That brings me to tip number four - ease the bloat.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:47.729
During the luteal phase of menstruation and leading in to those first few days of our period, it's very common feel bloated

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:55.620
regardless of how much or what you eat thanks to our higher levels of estrogen. And those estrogen levels cause us to retain more water.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:11:02.820
Therefore, as I mentioned earlier with the menstrual phase, you'll want to focus on more fresh foods instead of highly processed

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:03.960
salty foods.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:10.379
You might also want to to plain water as carbonated drinks can cause more gas and discomfort

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:18.449
plus going easy on foods that tend to cause you digestive distress. This obviously varies from person to person, but common triggers are

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:22.469
high FODMAP foods like dairy, apples, wheat, and beans.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.080
Gassy veggies like broccoli and kale,

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:32.279
sugar alcohols and booze. If you do have a higher sodium meal and are feeling a little bit uncomfortable, don't sweat it.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.790
I mean you can pair it with foods that are rich in water like cucumber,

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:42.000
lettuce and citrus, or potassium rich foods like bananas and sweet potatoes to help balance out the salt.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:48.659
Bottom line, us ladies deal with our monthly period every month, so we are totally experts right now.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:55.980
In fact, you're probably doing a lot of these things without even thinking about them because they intuitively just feel good.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:12:00.060
But if you're finding some of your symptoms at different times of the month totally throwing you off,

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:07.409
I hope this video gives you some evidence-based ideas on how you can feel your best no matter what your hormones throw at you.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:12.120
Well folks, that is all for today. As always, if you like this video be sure to give it a thumbs up,

